{"_format": "A fit manifest (typed-decision-models v1.3 §3.4; model-bench decisions.load_fit_manifest; impl review Pass 8, P8-m1) is the bytes of UTF-8 text: one input_hash per line, each a lowercase-hex sha256 (64 chars of [0-9a-f]), each line terminated by a single LF (the last included; no CR, no BOM), lines strictly ascending (sorted, no repeat). The empty file is the manifest of zero inputs. A candidate declares fitManifest.sha256 = sha256 over the file's raw bytes and fitManifest.size = the number of entries (never the byte length). Each row below: 'text' is the whole file, 'sha256'/'size' the candidate's declaration, 'accept' the verdict; an accepted row lists its 'entries'; a refused row names the 'rule' it breaks, and 'refusal' is a substring of model-bench's own error message (reader-side only). Every 'sha256' was computed by hand with printf ... | sha256sum, never by the code under test. U6's fit.py byte-copies this file and must write manifests the accepted rows describe."}
